          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong stochastic process
            describes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamical+system"} dynamical system
            evolving over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linearly+ordered+set"} linearly ordered set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time"}> time
            ”), typically taken to be the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"}> positive
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/laws+of+motion"} laws of motion
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            (or any other
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+monad"} probability monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras of that monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/expectation+value"} expected value
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurements"} measurements
            on that process.
          %p
            By a
            %strong random process
            physicists usually mean the same, but mathematicians sometimes allow random processes indexed by more general sets, not usually with meaning of time or equipped with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
          %p
            The most studied examples include
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brownian+motion"} Brownian motion
            %em
              %span.newWikiWord
                Ornstein-Uhlenbeck processes
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Ornstein-Uhlenbeck+processes"} ?
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Lévy processes
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/L%C3%A9vy+processes"} ?
            %strong indivisible stochastic process
            which
            %a{:href => "#Barendes25"} Barandes 2025
            has used to give an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indivisible+stochastic+process+interpretation+of+quantum+mechanics"} indivisible stochastic process interpretation of quantum mechanics
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            We define discrete time stochastic processes following
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lawvere62"} Lawvere 1962
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countably many
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1,2,...\}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Meas
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Meas}_G
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Meas
                    %mi G
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Meas}_G^{N}
            denote the category whose objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Omega}
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequences"} sequences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_0, \Omega_1,\ldots
            of objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Meas
                    %mi G
