          %p
            An
            %strong indivisible stochastic process
            is a stochastic process which is not divisible. Such processes are employed in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indivisible+stochastic+process+interpretation+of+quantum+mechanics"} indivisible stochastic process interpretation of quantum mechanics
          %p
            An indivisible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stochastic+process"} stochastic process
            is a very general type of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stochastic+process"} stochastic process
            which can exhibit wild behavior because, for any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
