            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel+space"} standard Borel space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\infty}
              is the one point compactification of the real line. (There is no
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(\mathbb{R}) \rightarrow \mathbb{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \xrightarrow{f} \mathbb{R}
              we first need to embedd
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              into
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\infty}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔼
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}_{\bullet}(id_{\mathbb{R}_{\infty}})
              is defined at each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \in G(\mathbb{R}_{\infty})
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔼
                        %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∫
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mn ∞
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi dP
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}_{P}(id_{\mathbb{R}_{\infty}}) =\int id_{\mathbb{R}_{\infty}} \, dP
            %p
              Note that measurements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \xrightarrow{f} X
              can be taken over any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              which lies in the category of algebras of the monad
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel+space"} standard Borel space
              the
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔼
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi id
                            %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(X) \xrightarrow{\mathbb{E}_{\bullet}(id_X)} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+algebras"} category of algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔼
                      %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}_{P}(id_X)
              is the unique element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that for all affine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+maps"} measurable maps
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi m
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \xrightarrow{m} \mathbb{R}_{\infty}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔼
                      %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi X
                    %mi m
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi dP
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    m(\mathbb{E}_P(id_X)) = \int_X m \, dP
            %p
              holds. (Every algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              necessarily possesses a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"} convex space
              structure. The case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X=\mathbb{R}_{\infty}
              is just a special case which trivially satisfies the above property since the affine maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi m
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\infty} \xrightarrow{m} \mathbb{R}_{\infty}
              are of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi λ
                    %mi r
                    %mo +
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(r) =\lambda r + t
              (scale + translate) and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔼
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}_{\bullet}(id_{\mathbb{R}_{\infty}})
              simplifies to the standard expectation operator. A derivation of the category of algebras for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel+space"} standard Borel space
              is given on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
              page.)
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Here are two elementary examples of an indivisible stochastic process due to
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Barendes25"} Barendes 2025
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+space"} finite space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega = \{1,2\}=\Omega_n
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi Q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mi n
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \xrightarrow{\tilde{Q}_n} \Omega
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mfrac
                                    %mrow
                                      %msubsup
                                        %mi t
                                        %mi n
                                        %mn 2
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi τ
                                        %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mfrac
                                    %mrow
                                      %msubsup
                                        %mi t
                                        %mi n
                                        %mn 2
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi τ
                                        %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mfrac
                                    %mrow
                                      %msubsup
                                        %mi t
                                        %mi n
                                        %mn 2
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi τ
                                        %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mfrac
                                    %mrow
                                      %msubsup
                                        %mi t
                                        %mi n
                                        %mn 2
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi τ
                                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde{Q}_n =  \begin{pmatrix} e^{-\frac{t_n^2}{\tau^2}} &amp; 1-e^{-\frac{t_n^2}{\tau^2}} \\ 1-e^{-\frac{t_n^2}{\tau^2}} &amp; e^{-\frac{t_n^2}{\tau^2}} \end{pmatrix}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_n
              is the time at stage
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              is a constant. (For a finite space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              a dynamic law
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \rightarrow \Omega
              can be represented by a matrix.)
            %p
              Similarly, on the same space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi cos
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ω
                              %msub
                                %mi t
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi sin
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ω
                              %msub
                                %mi t
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi sin
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ω
                              %msub
                                %mi t
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi cos
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ω
                              %msub
                                %mi t
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde{Q}_n =  \begin{pmatrix} \cos^2(\omega t_n) &amp; \sin^2(\omega t_n) \\ \sin^2(\omega t_n) &amp; \cos^2(\omega t_n) \end{pmatrix}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              is a constant.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stochastic_process"} stochastic process
            %li#Lawvere62
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                %em The Category of Probabilistic Mappings With Applications to Stochastic Processes, Statistics, and Pattern Recognition
                (1962), including abstract and commentary added by Lawvere in 2020,
                %a{:href => "https://lawverearchives.com"} Lawvere Archive
                (2025) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://lawverearchives.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/1962.probmap.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Xiao-qing Meng,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories of convex sets and of metric spaces with applications to stochastic programming and related areas
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Meng.djvu", :title => "Ph.D. thesis of Meng"} djvu
            %li#Barendes25
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Barandes"}> Jacob Barandes
                ,
                %em Quantum Systems as Indivisible Stochastic Processes
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.21192"}> arXiv:2507.21192
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            With an eye towards
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+noise"} quantum noise
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/St%C3%A9phane+Attal"}> Stéphane Attal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Stochastic Processes
              %em Lectures on Quantum Noises
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://math.univ-lyon1.fr/~attal/Stochastic_Processes.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.univ-lyon1.fr/~attal/chapters.html"} webpage
          %p
            On some kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            in stochastic PDEs:
          %ul
            %li
              Igor V. Ovchinnikov:
              %em Ubiquitous order known as chaos
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.17157"}> arXiv:2503.17157
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
